bcon: fix Kitty Unicode placeholders (U=1), as used by rmpc, yazi, ratatui-image

- a=T with U=1 created a real placement at the cursor and moved the cursor;
  it now only records a virtual placement.
- Virtual placements are sized from the image when c=/r= are omitted, and are
  no longer pruned (text writes, erase, scroll, clear) or drawn as real images.
- The row/column diacritics table was wrong (110 entries, 74 mismatching
  Kitty's); it is now Kitty's rowcolumn-diacritics.txt.
- Placeholder cells without diacritics inherit them from the left neighbour.
- Tiles are drawn in their own pass after the text flush, for every
  placeholder cell each frame, merged into one quad per run of cells.
